.TH WAITFOR 1 6/18/90
.CM 4
.SH NAME
waitfor \- wait for a system service to come up
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwaitfor\fP [\fBnetname\fP|\fBslot\fP slot-num]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fIwaitfor(1)\fR is used to wait for a system service to come up.
For example, a common usage is
.nf
.in +5n
.ft B
	snames &
	waitfor netname
	machid &
.fi
.in -5n
.ft R
which starts a name server, waits for the name service to come up,
and then starts a program which will use the name service.
If \fIwaitfor\fR were omitted, the program might start running
before the name server started.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
mach_ports_lookup(2), service_waitfor(3).
